  <name>Crowded tracks (Tree share)</name>
  <description>Every width-hungry track at once: long tip labels, a domain architecture per tip, an aligned sequence and a Color-by legend. The tree is allocated its share of the width FIRST and the tracks divide what is left, so it stays a tree instead of being squeezed to the line it used to collapse to. Drag the CONTROL PANEL&apos;s &quot;Tree share&quot; slider (under Node size) to re-divide it: the alignment is the elastic track and gives way first, while the labels, the clade bands and the legend column are never shaved -- half a legend still covers what it was meant to stand clear of. Switch OFF &quot;Shorten Labels&quot; to see the labels compete at full length -- it is on by default, so they open abbreviated. The domain zoom (d- / d+) trades against the alignment through the same budget. Works in every display type: the rectangular layouts divide the depth WIDTH, the circular one the tip-ring RADIUS, the unrooted one its fan spread.</description>
